[h1]R.A.T.S. Topographic Map[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]
[b]Bugs, ideas, questions:[/b] [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/topo]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]

[b]Stop flying blind over the terrain.[/b]
Land heights and sea depths on your tactical map: for low-level flying, terrain masking, radar horizons, and for knowing where your submarine has room to dive.

[h2]The highlights[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Heights and depths at a glance.[/b] Land tinted in 13 height bands, sea in 12 depth bands, with hill shading and contour lines that follow your zoom
[*][b]Terrain that hits back.[/b] Select an aircraft and every piece of terrain at or above its altitude is hatched red, with the clearance in the readout
[*][b]Submarine room to dive.[/b] Select a submarine and see where it is below the thermal layer, where the layer ends and where the water gets too shallow
[*][b]19 looks, day and night.[/b] ECDIS, Soviet General Staff map, survey sonar, phosphor green, amber display, red light and more. Make your own with a small text file
[*][b]Made for the 3D globe.[/b] Lined up with the stock map at every zoom, at high latitudes, across the date line and over the poles
[*]Height or depth under the mouse pointer in metres and feet, and it works in the mission editor too
[/list]

[h2]The looks[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Day:[/b] Standard, army tactical map, Soviet General Staff map, bathymetric chart, ECDIS (IHO S-52 colours), desert storm, satellite, 1940s chart, glacier
[*][b]Night:[/b] Midnight, Standard, Black, recon photo, survey sonar (depth as a rainbow), combat display, phosphor green, white phosphor, amber display, red light
[*][b]Your own:[/b] Save this look as a theme file, edit the small text file, and the map updates when you save
[/list]

[h2]How to use[/h2]
Open the map in a mission and the layer is already on. One menu button, the mountain mark, sits in the map's title bar, left of the map menu. Its list holds:
[list]
[*][b]Topography:[/b] the layer on or off (also F6)
[*][b]Look:[/b] the looks for the day or night map you are on (Shift+F6 jumps to the next one)
[*][b]Legend:[/b] the colour key and the contour step
[*][b]Cursor height:[/b] the readout next to the pointer
[/list]
In the mission editor the same menu button is at the top right of its map.

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]The heights and depths are the ones the simulation uses, from the game's own terrain data, including the terrain height multiplier and under-water depth factor in Options, World
[*]The mission area and the world are drawn once at mission start, so nothing is redrawn while you play zoomed out
[*]Unit symbols, waypoints and labels stay on top. No game files are changed
[*]Works together with Better TacMap
[/list]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Everything is in [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\config\dev.sewerlabs.seapowertopo.cfg[/i], created on first start. You can edit it with the game open; changes show on the next redraw.
[list]
[*]Toggle key and look key, looks for the day and night map, opacity, hill shading strength
[*]Contour lines and interval, where the height and depth bands start, sea tint, chart safety contour
[*]Red terrain highlight for aircraft, thermal layer for submarines
[*]Height under cursor (WithOverlay, Always or Off), units in metres, feet or both, the Legend entry
[*]Overlay resolution and pre-drawing of the mission area and the world
[/list]
Theme files: [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\config\SeaPowerTopo\themes[/i] holds one .ini per look, for example [i]Base=black[/i] and [i]LandLines=170,150,120[/i] for Black with warm contour lines. Every key is explained in the [i]_example.ini[/i] and in [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerTopo/blob/main/docs/themes.md]docs/themes.md[/url].

[h2]Install and game versions[/h2]
[b]R.A.T.S. Keel[/b] is required: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3835527459]subscribe[/url] and switch it on in the Mods menu; its page has the one install step. It replaces Anchor Chain.
Run in the game on the 3D globe public beta (build 261107). The build for 0.8.7 (flat map) has the same features and passes the offline checks; the item has a build for each and the right one switches on by itself. The screenshots are from the globe version.

[h2]Problems, feedback, ideas[/h2]
Post bugs, feedback and ideas on the [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/topo]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]. For a bug, add [i]<Sea Power>\BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/i] (as a link).

Source code (MIT): [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerTopo]github.com/struckl/SeaPowerTopo[/url]

